# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dotfile policy (this file)
# Everything dot-prefixed is local state: .venv, .streamlit secrets, editor state, caches.
.*
# ...except the dotfiles a public repo is supposed to carry. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT directory is excluded, so `.github/` and `.streamlit/` are re-included before their
# contents. Without this, `git add -A` silently skips a CI workflow (the checklist claims CI runs
# the contract tests) and the Streamlit theme config the app boots with.
!.github/
!.github/**
!.gitattributes
!.dockerignore
!.python-version
!.gcloudignore
# `.streamlit/` IS re-included: the theme config the app boots with is public and carries no
# secrets (tests/test_gitignore_policy.py checks its content for secret-shaped keys). Streamlit's
# documented secrets location is `.streamlit/secrets.toml`, which stays ignored below — the order
# is load-bearing, because the last matching rule wins.
!.streamlit/
!.streamlit/config.toml
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# `.gitignore` matches its own `.*` rule, which means it is untracked-but-ignored and `git add -A`
# silently skips it: the published repo would ship with NO ignore rules and no protection for
# `.env`, `data/raw/` or a stray `.h5`. Re-included explicitly, like the entries above.
!.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local/personal + tool caches
.*.local
.*cache
*cache*
AGENTS.md
agents.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/agents.md
.agents/
.opencode/
.impeccable/
docs/opencode_pack/
**/skills/
**/*PROMPT*.md
**/*prompt*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- internal docs stay local
# The submitted repository ships only the reader-facing entry point (README.md), the runtime science
# guide (docs/science-guide.md, read by `load_documented_limits` for Tab 4) and the pitch figures.
# Design decisions, runbooks, hand-offs, verification logs and work requests stay in each
# contributor's checkout: they explain how the project was built, not what it does.
CONTEXT.md
flujo_trabajo_y_responsabilidades.md
deploy/README.md
pipeline/README.md
pipeline/ingest/README.md
docs/*.md
!docs/science-guide.md
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
venv/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- never version heavy downloads
# (flujo §3.2); only the small data/processed summaries are committed, under the 15 MB budget.
data/raw/
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.he5
*.nc
*.zip
*.tif
*.tiff
*.part
*.SAFE/

# staging sidecars (e.g. land_use.csv from enrich_context.py) live here, deliberately outside the
# case directories so pipeline/validate_artifacts.py does not reject a case for holding a 5th file
data/staging/

# download backstops. Granules normally land only in data/raw/ (above), but a file moved or resumed
# outside it must never be committed: one NISAR GUNW is ~GBs and cannot be undone from history.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- credentials / local overrides
# Earthdata session cookies / credentials (dotfiles are already covered by `.*`, this is the
# non-dot name people actually use)
cookies.txt
.env
.env.*
# ...and the documented template that must ship. This negation is AFTER `.env.*` on purpose: git
# applies the last matching rule, so a blanket `.env.*` would otherwise hide the one dotfile the
# README tells a new contributor to copy.
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OS / editor cruft
skills-lock.json
reports/
tmp/
*.log
*.geojson.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local scratch that must never be committed
# pytest's tmp_path base when TMPDIR points inside the repo (it reached 114 GB here), matplotlib's
# figure dump and the pitch deck are working artefacts, not inputs: `git add -A` must not see them,
# because a directory that size cannot be undone from history. `/test` is anchored so it cannot
# shadow a future `test/` directory.
pytest-of-*/
make-figures-mpl-*/
SAR_PITCH_PPT.pptx
/test
# The role contract stays local: it is the project's working agreement, not part of the published
# repo. The file is tracked nowhere and read by every contributor from their own checkout.
AGENTS.md
